      "h": 752,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "t": "p",
          "text": "Surface tokens define the substrate fill that sits beneath elevated content. They control the canvas color a card, dialog, popover, or panel rests on, ensuring consistent figure–ground separation in both light and dark modes.\n\nPair a surface token with a shadow/* effect style to lift the surface off the page.\n\nScope: this page documents elevational surfaces only. Non-elevational surface tokens — surface/base, surface/background, surface/inverse, surface/scrim, surface/hover, surface/active, surface/muted, and the surface/feedback/* family — are documented on the Color page.",
          "style": "Body/Body M"
        },
